    "details": "The nginx developers report:\n\n> A buffer overflow might occur in a worker process when using the\n> \\\"alias\\\" directive if the request URI was changed by the \\\"rewrite\\\"\n> directive and was then mapped to a file path (CVE-2026-15176).\n>\n> A buffer overflow might occur in a worker process while evaluating\n> string expressions with variables, which affected the document root\n> calculation and request logging in the http and stream modules\n> (CVE-2026-93479).\n>\n> When using HTTP/3 a part of an unknown frame might be treated as the\n> request body, which might result in bypassing the\n> \\\"client_max_body_size\\\" limit or injecting data in the proxied\n> request (CVE-2026-95101).\n>\n> When using TLS session ticket key rotation, one of the keys was left\n> uninitialized, which might allow to forge a session (CVE-2026-97629).\n>\n> When using asynchronous file I/O (AIO), use-after-free might occur in\n> certain configurations if the SSI page has \\\"include virtual\\\"\n> commands (CVE-2026-97205).\n",
    "id": "FreeBSD-2026-0514",
